From df00787d97dc51e120f4ee7a790e28be056e92fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 06:37:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] fix: dealer notifications page crash - genuinely
 missing import, not a mystery bug

Found the definitive root cause this time (previous investigation
couldn't pin it down without console access): timeAgoLong was called
on every real notification but never imported anywhere in this file -
a plain ReferenceError. Checked all 4 role-specific notification
pages for the same pattern - only the dealer one had it (staff and
partner correctly import it, super-admin doesn't use it at all).

This also explains 'it was showing before' exactly: with zero
notifications, the .map() that calls timeAgoLong never executes, so
the page rendered fine on an empty list. The moment a real
notification existed to render, it crashed immediately - matching the
timing of when this started being reported. The error boundary from
earlier in this engagement caught it correctly and prevented it from
taking down the whole dashboard, exactly as designed - but this fixes
the actual underlying crash rather than just containing it.
